{ In all these diagrams, we have a position where each side has the same piece (N vs. N , B vs. B , R vs R). White is a pawn up, and the defender's piece is blocking the enemy passed pawn. In each case, the blockade of the passed pawn can't be broken.

Let's compare the following Kingless diagram with the previous three... } { [%csl Be8,Bd7,Be6,Bd5,Be4,Bd3,Bd1,Bd2,Be1,Be2,Be3,Bd4,Be5,Bd6,Be7,Bd8] }
